{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/planarity\/planarembedding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Planarity"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlanarEmbedding"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbeddingV","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding.swift#L67","fileName":"PlanarEmbedding.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"PlanarEmbedding"},"abstract":[{"text":"A planar embedding of a graph: a rotation system, the clockwise order of the edges around each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, over every edge position (NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"PlanarEmbedding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", LEMON’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"PlanarEmbedding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"OGDF’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"CombinatorialEmbedding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Its faces satisfy Euler’s formula, n − m + f = 2, in every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connected component with an edge.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A self-loop appears twice in its vertex’s order, its two ends adjacent, enclosing a face of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length 1. Parallel copies sit side by side, each consecutive pair enclosing a face of length 2.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each clockwise order starts at the first edge of ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Faces."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The face after the half-edge from u along edge e to w continues with the half-edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before e in the clockwise order at w (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next_face_half_edge"},{"type":"text","text":"), so a face lies to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right of each of its half-edges. Faces are counted per connected component, and an isolated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex has none: two disjoint triangles have four faces."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The embedding keeps the graph it was made from (copy-on-write, so O(1)); mutating the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"afterwards does not change it. When a graph has several embeddings, which one is returned is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not specified, but it depends only on the graph’s rows: graphs with the same vertices, the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge positions and the same incidence order get the same embedding."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s23